Kilómetro Cero — 3D circuit mode
================================

This directory is a derivative work, separate from the Phaser game at the root
of this repository. This NOTICE records what was inherited, what was added, and
what was removed. See ../NOTICE for the root project.


1. UPSTREAM WORK
----------------

The 3D mode is derived from:

    react-racing-game
    https://github.com/colyseus/react-racing-game
    Licensed under the MIT License

which is itself a fork of:

    @pmndrs/racing-game
    Copyright 2021 pmndrs, contributors
    https://github.com/pmndrs/racing-game
    Licensed under the MIT License

The upstream repository was cloned into this directory and its .git removed.
Everything here that is not listed in section 4 descends from that project — in
particular the React Three Fiber application shell: the chase/first-person/
bird's-eye cameras, the dust, skid, boost and engine-audio effects, the zustand
store and key bindings, and the whole HUD (clock, speedometer, help, colour
picker, minimap, leaderboard).

The upstream @react-three/cannon raycast-vehicle physics has been REMOVED
entirely, together with the cannon collision world (road trimesh, wall boxes,
lap trigger volumes, killzone). The car is now an analytic four-corner vehicle
model adapted from APEX FORMULA 2026 (see section 2), living in the track
frame of the measured circuit; walls and lap timing are analytic too. The
chase camera's behaviour is also no longer upstream's. README.md records the
history.

The upstream MIT licence text is reproduced verbatim in LICENSE.md and continues
to govern this work. The typo in its copyright line ("pmdrs") is upstream's; it
is left untouched.


